(Title) Tj
T*
(Bactericidal Activity and Tolerability of Novel Combination Therapy in Drug-Resistant) Tj
T*
(Tuberculosis: A Pharmacodynamic Investigation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Patients with rifampicin-resistant tuberculosis \(RR-TB\) require intensive multi-drug) Tj
T*
(regimens. We assessed the bactericidal effectiveness and safety profile of a four-drug) Tj
T*
(combination therapy compared with conventional treatment in a cohort of RR-TB patients) Tj
T*
(enrolled across two treatment centers. Participants received the investigational regimen) Tj
T*
(as part of a treatment protocol implemented in clinical settings in Eastern Europe and) Tj
T*
(South Africa. Sputum smear conversion and bacterial load reduction were measured at) Tj
T*
(defined intervals. The investigational combination achieved approximately 18% higher) Tj
T*
(bacillary clearance compared to standard therapy in the overall population, with) Tj
T*
(particularly strong results in patients without severe systemic disease. However,) Tj
T*
(accelerated bacterial reduction was observed in only a subset of patients. Hematologic) Tj
T*
(complications, including anemia and reduced neutrophil counts, were more prevalent among) Tj
T*
(those receiving higher cumulative drug exposure, though these did not necessitate) Tj
T*
(treatment discontinuation in most cases. The clinical findings support the use of this) Tj
T*
(intensive multi-drug approach as a viable treatment option for patients with resistance to) Tj
T*
(first-line agents.) Tj
ET
